---
import { withBase } from '../../utils/paths';
import '../../styles/experiment/fonts.css';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8" /><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" /><meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow" /><title>TKG — Compare timeline experiments</title></head><body>
  <main><img class="logo" src={withBase('images/branding/tkg-logo.png', base)} alt="The Known Galaxy" width="2299" height="894" /><p class="status">Local design experiment · production is unchanged</p><h1>Two ways to read history.</h1><p class="intro">The same records and controls. Two different approaches to the timeline and historical record.</p>
  <div class="concepts"><article><span class="concept-letter">A</span><h2>Refined existing design</h2><p>Boxed records and cleaner typography, now paired with B’s image-first expanded record. The familiar timeline stays; images sit above the narrative and metadata.</p><a class="primary" href={withBase('concept-a/',base)}>Explore Concept A →</a><p><a href={`${withBase('concept-a/',base)}?demo=gallery#fixture-major`}>Review A’s multi-image gallery example →</a></p></article><article><span class="concept-letter">B</span><h2>Reimagined timeline</h2><p>A continuous field of time, with open labels attached to year anchors. Major moments carry the hierarchy; imagery and narrative lead the expanded record.</p><a class="primary" href={withBase('concept-b/',base)}>Explore Concept B →</a></article></div>
  <section class="details"><h2>What to compare</h2><p>Choose Neutral, Jedi or Sith in either header. Perspective keeps every event visible and preserves your current selection. Until faction accounts are written, the record clearly falls back to Neutral.</p><p>Use the “Title face” selector to compare Source Serif 4, Libre Baskerville and Noto Serif with Ubuntu controls and body text.</p><p><a href={withBase('compare/screenshots/',base)}>View desktop, tablet, mobile and record screenshots →</a></p><h3>Cluster and gallery test</h3><p>These links add explicitly synthetic layout fixtures to the real records. Gallery images are supplied game-interface references, not historical evidence. Fixtures never appear on the production route.</p><div class="test-links"><a href={`${withBase('concept-a/',base)}?demo=clusters#fixture-major`}>Test A: clusters + gallery</a><a href={`${withBase('concept-b/',base)}?demo=clusters#fixture-major`}>Test B: clusters + gallery</a></div></section>
  <section class="details"><h2>Weekly event density preview</h2><p>Four total records per year from 15–25 ABD: 44 records in that interval, including existing approved events. Added examples are marked as test content. Other existing events remain visible.</p><p><a href={`${withBase('concept-a/',base)}?demo=density`}>Review Concept A with four events per canonical year →</a></p><p>Every year now gets 450px, including empty years. At this density, A's compact timeline fits into four rows and a 600px canvas, down from 850px before the vertical compaction and 15 rows / 2,982px at the original year spacing. Each event remains individually clickable.</p><p><a href={`${withBase('concept-a/',base)}?demo=density-five`}>Review five-event months from 37–65 ABD →</a></p></section>
  <footer><a href={withBase('',base)}>View unchanged production-style route</a><span>Experimental branch · no deployment</span></footer></main>
</body></html>
<style>
  :global(*){box-sizing:border-box} :global(body){margin:0;background:#06090d;color:#e8edf2;font-family:Ubuntu,'Segoe UI',sans-serif} main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:54px clamp(24px,5vw,60px)} .logo{width:190px;height:auto;display:block;margin-bottom:32px}.status{color:#96a9bc;font-size:13px}h1,h2,h3{font-family:'Source Serif 4',Georgia,serif;font-weight:400}h1{font-size:clamp(36px,5vw,58px);line-height:1.1;margin:20px 0}h2{font-size:28px;margin:16px 0}h3{font-size:23px}.intro{font-size:18px;line-height:1.8;color:#bbc8d4;max-width:700px}.concepts{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:60px;margin:52px 0}.concepts article{border-top:1px solid #34475a;padding-top:28px}.concept-letter{color:#86aed1;font-size:20px}.concepts p,.details p{color:#aebfcd;font-size:16px;line-height:1.8}.primary{display:inline-block;background:#2875dc;color:white;padding:14px 18px;border-radius:2px;text-decoration:none;margin-top:16px}a{color:#a6c9ec}a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #8fc2ff;outline-offset:5px}.details{border-top:1px solid #293743;padding-top:24px;max-width:850px}.test-links{display:flex;gap:28px;flex-wrap:wrap}footer{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:54px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid #293743;font-size:13px;color:#91a4b5}@media(max-width:650px){.concepts{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:40px;margin:36px 0}}
</style>
